insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-5460fd26a306', 'en', 'B1', 'The Homework Debate: What Should Schools Do?', 'In many Brazilian schools, homework is a big part of student life. Every week, teachers give assignments for students to do at home. Some students enjoy this, but others think it is too much. Recently, a group of parents in São Paulo asked the school to reduce the amount of homework. They said that their children were too tired and had no time to play. This started a big discussion about the value of homework.

Many teachers believe that homework is important for learning. They say that it helps students practice what they learned in class. "Students must review the lessons at home," says Mrs. Oliveira, a math teacher. "They should not forget everything after school. Homework is a way to fix the knowledge in their minds." Teachers also think that homework teaches responsibility and discipline. These are important skills for the future.

However, some experts disagree. They argue that too much homework can be harmful. According to a recent study, students who spend many hours on homework may feel stressed and anxious. "Children must have time to relax and play," says psychologist Dr. Souza. "They need to sleep well and exercise. If they only study, they may have health problems." Some experts also believe that homework is not effective for young children. They say that play is more important at that age.

The discussion also includes the families'' role. Many parents want to help their children, but they do not know how. Some say that the homework is too difficult, and they cannot explain it to their kids. "I didn''t study this in school," says one father. "I can''t help my son with his homework. It must be simpler." Others think that homework is a way to see what their children are learning. "I like homework because it shows me what my kids study," says a mother.

So, what could be the solution? Some schools are trying a new approach. They are giving less homework, but they are making it more interesting. For example, instead of writing exercises, students need to read a book and talk about it in class. Or they might do a project at home with their family. This way, homework becomes a fun activity, not a boring task. Teachers are also trying to be flexible. They know that each student is different, so they offer optional assignments.

In the end, the most important thing is balance. Homework should not take all the free time from students, but it should also help them learn. As a student, you must speak up. If you feel that the homework is too much, you should talk to your teacher. Remember, you are part of the discussion. Your voice matters.

So, what do you think? Does homework help you learn? Or is it just a waste of time? Maybe it can be both. The school is thinking about new rules, and they want to hear from the students. Perhaps you can suggest a change.', '[{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz que muitos professores acreditam que o dever de casa ajuda a praticar o conteúdo e ensina responsabilidade e disciplina.","options":["Because it helps students practice and learn responsibility.","Because parents ask for homework.","Because homework is always fun.","Because students love doing homework."],"prompt":"According to the text, why do many teachers support homework?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona que especialistas acreditam que muito dever de casa pode causar estresse e ansiedade, e que as crianças precisam de tempo para relaxar e brincar.","options":["Students might have no time for hobbies.","Students might learn too much.","Parents might not help.","Teachers might get tired."],"prompt":"What problem do some experts see with too much homework?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto cita um pai que diz: \"Não estudei isso na escola. Não posso ajudar meu filho com o dever de casa. Deve ser mais simples.\" Isso mostra que os pais muitas vezes não entendem a matéria.","options":["They think homework is not important.","They do not understand the material.","They are too busy.","They do not like the teachers."],"prompt":"According to the text, why do some parents not help with homework?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz: \"Algumas escolas estão tentando uma nova abordagem. Eles estão dando menos dever de casa, mas estão tornando-o mais interessante.\" E também fala em flexibilidade, como opções.","options":["Giving more homework than before.","Parent involvement in class.","More interesting and flexible homework.","No homework at all."],"prompt":"What is one new approach some schools are trying?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz: \"Se você sente que o dever de casa é demais, você deve conversar com seu professor.\"","options":["Stop doing homework.","Talk to their teachers.","Complain to their parents.","Work harder."],"prompt":"According to the passage, what should students do if they have too much homework?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto apresenta diferentes pontos de vista sobre o dever de casa (professores, especialistas, pais) e conclui que o mais importante é o equilíbrio.","options":["Homework should be banned.","Homework is always harmful.","There are different views about homework, and a balance is needed.","Brazilian schools have no homework."],"prompt":"What is the main idea of the text?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
