insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-8d9e1d282471', 'en', 'B1', 'Deciding What to Do: Gerunds and Infinitives', 'Have you ever stopped to think about how we express choices and preferences? In English, we often use gerunds (verbs ending in -ing) and infinitives (to + verb) to talk about actions. This can be tricky for learners because sometimes both are correct, but the meaning changes. Let''s explore this with a story.

Maria is a student from São Paulo who is spending a year in California. She loves learning new things, but she sometimes struggles to decide what to do on weekends. Last Saturday, she wanted to go to the beach, but she also considered visiting a museum. She decided to go hiking instead because she enjoys being outdoors.

At the hiking trail, she met John, an American student. He suggested taking a break near the river. While they were resting, John said, "I really like to try new activities, but I hate getting up early on Saturdays." Maria laughed and replied, "I don''t mind waking up early, but I avoid going out alone. That''s why I joined this hiking group."

John told her about a photography club that meets every Sunday. "You might enjoy taking pictures," he said. "I''ve been thinking about joining it." Maria was interested, but she remembered that she had promised to call her mother. She said, "I need to call my mom every Sunday. She expects me to keep in touch."

John nodded and said, "That''s important. You should keep calling her. But you could also join us after your call. We usually start at 3 PM." Maria thought it was a good idea. She agreed to meet him in front of the library at 2:45 PM.

On Sunday, Maria arrived on time. She felt a bit nervous, but John was there to introduce her to the others. They were all very friendly. The leader, a professional photographer, said, "I hope you enjoy taking photos with us. Remember, the goal is to have fun and to improve your skills."

After the meeting, Maria realized that she had made a new group of friends. She was happy that she had decided to join. She thought, "I''ll continue coming here every week. It''s a great way to practice English and to explore my creativity."

Now Maria knows that whether you choose to use a gerund or an infinitive, it''s important to express your intentions clearly. And sometimes, the best decisions are the ones you make without thinking too much.', '[{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"No texto, ela decidiu ir caminhar (hiking) em vez de ir à praia ou ao museu.","options":["She went to the beach.","She visited a museum.","She went hiking.","She stayed home."],"prompt":"What did Maria decide to do last Saturday?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"Depois de ''enjoy'', usamos gerúndio (-ing). Portanto, ''being'' é um gerúndio.","options":["Gerund after enjoy","Infinitive after enjoy","Gerund after decide","Infinitive after decide"],"prompt":"Which verb pattern is used in ''she enjoys being outdoors''?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"John disse ''I hate getting up early on Saturdays'', então ele odeia acordar cedo.","options":["He loves it.","He hates it.","He doesn''t mind it.","He avoids it."],"prompt":"What did John say about getting up early?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Ela lembrou que tinha prometido ligar para a mãe e que precisava manter contato.","options":["She didn''t like photography.","She had to call her mother.","She had to go to work.","She was too tired."],"prompt":"Why didn''t Maria join the photography club immediately?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Ela pensou ''I''ll continue coming here every week'', então ela planeja continuar indo.","options":["She will stop going to the club.","She will continue coming every week.","She will join another club.","She will go back to Brazil."],"prompt":"What does Maria plan to do after the meeting?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Lembrar de fazer algo (remember to do) significa não esquecer de fazer. A opção mais próxima é ''I don''t forget to call my mother''.","options":["I remember calling my mother.","I don''t forget to call my mother.","I forgot calling my mother.","I remember to have called my mother."],"prompt":"Which sentence has the same meaning as ''I remember to call my mother''?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, body=excluded.body, questions=excluded.questions, is_published=excluded.is_published, updated_at=now();

insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-3e962b2f53ee', 'en', 'B1', 'Everyday Phrasal Verbs: Taking Off and Finding Out', 'Phrasal verbs are a big part of everyday English. They are verbs combined with prepositions or adverbs, like ''give up'' or ''look after''. Learning them can make you sound more natural and help you understand conversations better. In this lesson, we will explore some common phrasal verbs that are useful in daily life: ''take off'', ''find out'', ''give up'', ''look after'', ''run into'', and ''put off''.

Consider how these phrasal verbs are used. ''Take off'' can mean to remove something (like clothes), or it can mean for a plane to leave the ground. For example, I took off my jacket because it was hot. The plane took off on time. ''Find out'' means to discover information. You might find out the answer to a question, or find out that a friend is moving away. For instance, I found out that the store closes at 9 PM.

''Give up'' is a common phrasal verb that means to stop trying or to stop doing something. You can give up smoking, give up a hobby, or give up on a difficult task. After many failed attempts, she gave up learning the guitar. ''Look after'' means to take care of someone or something. Parents look after their children, and you can look after a friend''s pet while they are away. My neighbor looks after my cat when I travel.

When you ''run into'' someone, you meet them by chance. It''s surprising to run into an old friend at the supermarket. This phrasal verb is often used for unexpected meetings. Another useful phrasal verb is ''put off'', which means to postpone or delay something. Because of the rain, they put off the picnic until Saturday. Many students put off doing their homework until the last minute.

In a story, these phrasal verbs can be very expressive. Imagine this: Sarah was at the airport. Her flight was delayed, and she was worried about running into her ex-boyfriend. She tried to find out the new departure time. She called her mother to ask if her mother could look after her dog for the weekend. After the call, she decided not to put off her trip any longer. Finally, the plane took off, and she felt relieved. She gave up her fear of flying and enjoyed the journey.

To master phrasal verbs, it''s important to see them in context and practice using them. Try to notice phrasal verbs in movies, songs, and conversations. Keep a list and write example sentences. With time, they will become a natural part of your English vocabulary.', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Quando falamos de avião, ''take off'' significa decolar, ou seja, sair do chão.","options":["To remove clothes","To leave the ground","To delay a flight","To arrive at a destination"],"prompt":"What does ''take off'' mean when talking about a plane?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"''Find out'' significa descobrir ou obter informação.","options":["give up","look after","find out","run into"],"prompt":"Which phrasal verb means ''to discover information''?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''Run into'' significa encontrar alguém por acaso, sem planejar.","options":["You chased them","You met them by chance","You avoided them","You invited them"],"prompt":"If you ''run into'' someone, what happened?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"''Put off'' significa adiar, transferir para depois.","options":["To postpone","To cancel","To start","To finish"],"prompt":"What does ''put off'' mean?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"''Look after'' significa cuidar de alguém ou algo.","options":["look after","take off","give up","put off"],"prompt":"Which phrasal verb means ''to take care of''?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''Give up'' significa desistir, parar de tentar ou fazer algo.","options":["To continue","To stop trying","To offer something","To begin again"],"prompt":"What does ''give up'' most closely mean?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, body=excluded.body, questions=excluded.questions, is_published=excluded.is_published, updated_at=now();

insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-c260bf350b72', 'en', 'B1', 'Recent Changes in My Hometown', 'Have you ever wondered how your hometown has changed over the years? I have lived in the same town for most of my life, and I have seen many transformations. When I was a child, the town was small and quiet. The streets were not busy, and everyone knew each other. But in the last ten years, the town has grown a lot. New shops and restaurants have opened, and more people have moved here. However, some things have not changed. The old park in the center, for example, has remained the same since I was young. I have visited it many times, but it still brings back good memories.

Last month, the mayor announced a new project to build a modern shopping mall. This has excited some residents, but others are worried about the traffic. I think the mall will be good for the economy, but we need to be careful. In the past, the town had a factory that closed down. Many people lost their jobs, and the town was sad for a while. But since then, the town has recovered, and new businesses have started. I have seen the unemployment rate drop, and I have felt the positive energy.

One thing that has changed a lot is the use of technology. When I was a teenager, I used to write letters to my friends. Now, I send messages on my phone. I have also learned to use video calls to talk to my family who live far away. My grandmother has never used a smartphone, but she has learned to use the computer a little. She told me that she has seen many inventions in her life, but the internet is the most amazing.

Another change is the environment. In the past, people did not recycle much. I remember that we threw everything in one bin. But today, recycling is common, and the town has become cleaner. A few years ago, the city council planted more trees, and the air has improved. I have noticed that there are more birds in the park now. It is nice to see these positive changes.

Of course, not every change has been good. The cost of living has increased a lot. Renting an apartment now is much more expensive than it was five years ago. Also, the traffic has become worse because there are more cars. But I have adapted to these changes. I have started to use the bus more often, and I have saved money by cooking at home.

Overall, I believe that change is a part of life. It can bring both problems and opportunities. I have learned to accept it and make the best of it. I hope that in the future, the town will continue to develop, but I also hope that we will not forget our history. After all, the past has shaped who we are today.', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O autor diz: ''When I was a child, the town was small and quiet.'' Portanto, a opção correta é ''It was small and quiet.''","options":["It was busy and modern.","It was small and quiet.","It had many shopping malls.","It was polluted and dirty."],"prompt":"What did the town look like when the author was a child?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona: ''In the past, the town had a factory that closed down.'' Portanto, a opção correta é ''It closed down.''","options":["It became a shopping mall.","It moved to another town.","It closed down.","It increased production."],"prompt":"What happened to the factory in the past?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O autor diz: ''Now, I send messages on my phone. I have also learned to use video calls to talk to my family.'' Portanto, a opção correta é ''They use phone messages and video calls.''","options":["They write more letters.","They use phone messages and video calls.","They talk less to friends.","They use smoke signals."],"prompt":"How has the author changed the way they communicate?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O autor afirma: ''recycling is common, and the town has become cleaner.'' Portanto, a opção correta é ''Recycling is now common.''","options":["More factories have been built.","Recycling is now common.","The traffic has improved.","Cars are banned."],"prompt":"What positive change in the environment does the author mention?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O autor menciona: ''The cost of living has increased a lot.'' Portanto, a opção correta é ''The cost of living has increased.''","options":["The town has become quieter.","The cost of living has increased.","The park has disappeared.","The bus service has stopped."],"prompt":"What negative change does the author mention?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O autor conclui: ''I believe that change is a part of life. It can bring both problems and opportunities.'' Portanto, a opção correta é ''Change can bring both problems and opportunities.''","options":["Change is always bad.","Change can bring both problems and opportunities.","Change never happens.","Change is only positive."],"prompt":"According to the text, what has the author learned about change?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
on conflict (id) do update set title=excluded.title, body=excluded.body, questions=excluded.questions, is_published=excluded.is_published, updated_at=now();

insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-7c39e1be39b3', 'en', 'B1', 'A Day to Remember: The Storm and the Rescue', 'Last summer, I had an experience that I will never forget. My friends and I decided to go camping near a beautiful lake in the mountains. We were all excited because the weather had been perfect for weeks. We packed our bags, drove for three hours, and arrived at the campsite in the late afternoon. While we were setting up our tents, the sky suddenly became dark. Thick clouds covered the sun, and a cold wind started to blow. We didn''t know it yet, but a big storm was coming our way.

We continued to prepare our camp, not paying much attention to the changing weather. We were laughing and telling stories when the first drops of rain fell. At first, it was just a light drizzle, but within minutes, it turned into a heavy downpour. We ran to our car to take shelter. As we were sitting inside, we saw lightning flash across the sky, and thunder roared loudly. The rain was falling so hard that we could barely see the trees around us.

After about thirty minutes, the rain stopped as quickly as it had started. We got out of the car and looked at our campsite. Everything was wet, and our tents were full of water. We were disappointed because we thought our trip would be ruined. But then, we noticed something amazing. A beautiful rainbow appeared, stretching across the sky. It was so colorful and bright that we forgot about our problems for a moment.

Later, while we were trying to dry our things, we heard a strange noise coming from the forest. It sounded like a small animal crying. We followed the sound and found a little puppy, shivering and alone. It looked scared and hungry. We gave it some food and water, and it immediately calmed down. We decided to take the puppy with us and look for its owner. We called it Lucky, because we felt lucky to have found it.

The next day, we went to a nearby village to ask if anyone knew about the puppy. A kind old man told us that the puppy belonged to his neighbor, who had been searching for it since the storm. We returned the puppy to its grateful owner, who thanked us with tears in his eyes. We felt so happy that we could help. Even though our camping trip wasn''t what we expected, it turned out to be an unforgettable adventure.

Now, whenever I see a rainbow, I remember that day and the little puppy we rescued. It taught me that sometimes, when things don''t go as planned, something even better can happen. We might have lost our camping gear, but we gained a wonderful memory and a new friend, even if only for a day. That experience made me realize the importance of helping others and staying positive in difficult situations.', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz: ''While we were setting up our tents, the sky suddenly became dark.'' Portanto, eles estavam montando as barracas quando o tempo mudou.","options":["They were packing their bags.","They were setting up their tents.","They were driving to the lake.","They were swimming in the lake."],"prompt":"What were the friends doing when the weather changed?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto afirma: ''We ran to our car to take shelter.'' Eles correram para o carro para se abrigar.","options":["They continued to prepare the camp.","They went for a walk.","They ran to their car.","They took photos of the storm."],"prompt":"What did the friends do when it started to rain heavily?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona: ''But then, we noticed something amazing. A beautiful rainbow appeared, stretching across the sky.''","options":["A beautiful rainbow","A group of birds","A forest fire","A clear blue sky"],"prompt":"What did the friends see after the rain stopped?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz: ''While we were trying to dry our things, we heard a strange noise coming from the forest... We followed the sound and found a little puppy.''","options":["In the lake","In the forest","In their car","In the village"],"prompt":"Where did the friends find the puppy?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto afirma: ''A kind old man told us that the puppy belonged to his neighbor, who had been searching for it since the storm.''","options":["The old man","A neighbor of the old man","One of the friends","A farmer"],"prompt":"Who did the puppy belong to?"},{"answer_index":3,"explanation_pt_br":"Na conclusão, o autor diz: ''It taught me that sometimes, when things don''t go as planned, something even better can happen... I realized the importance of helping others and staying positive.''","options":["To never go camping again","To always check the weather forecast","To be more careful with their belongings","To help others and stay positive"],"prompt":"What lesson did the author learn from this experience?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
