insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-c971ec4a01a7', 'en', 'B1', 'From Past to Future: A Story of Change and Resilience', 'In the small town of Vila Nova, Brazil, there was a bakery that had been owned by the same family for over 80 years. It was a place where locals gathered to buy fresh bread and share news. However, in recent years, the bakery began to struggle. A large supermarket opened nearby, selling cheaper bread, and many customers stopped coming. The owner, Sr. Carlos, was sad to see his family''s legacy fading. He knew he had to do something to save the bakery.

First, he tried to reduce costs by buying cheaper ingredients, but the bread didn''t taste as good, and even loyal customers complained. Then, he thought about closing the business, but he couldn''t imagine doing anything else. One day, his daughter, Ana, who had studied marketing in São Paulo, came to visit. She had an idea: ''Why don''t we use social media to attract more customers? We can show people how we make our bread and share the story of our bakery.''

Initially, Sr. Carlos was skeptical. He didn''t understand why anyone would be interested in a simple bakery on the internet. However, he decided to give it a try. They started posting videos of bread-making and photos of the old oven, which had been in the family for generations. To his surprise, the videos became popular. People from other cities started to visit, and the bakery began to get busy again.

But the real turning point happened when a local news channel featured their story. After the report aired, many people came to the bakery, and orders for special events started to arrive. Ana suggested they create a website to take online orders. This was a big change, as the bakery had never even had a phone before. Despite the challenges, they managed to adapt.

Now, the bakery is thriving. Sr. Carlos feels proud that he didn''t give up. He learned that sometimes you need to try new things, even if they seem scary at first. The bakery''s story is a good example of how small businesses can use modern tools to survive in a competitive market. As for the future, Sr. Carlos plans to pass the business to Ana, who has many innovative ideas. He is confident that the bakery will continue to be a part of the town''s history for many more years.

The story of this bakery teaches us that tradition and innovation can go hand in hand. By embracing change, we can preserve what matters most while also building a sustainable future. For Sr. Carlos, the bakery is not just a business; it is a symbol of his family''s hard work and dedication. He hopes that his grandchildren will also learn to value their heritage and adapt to the times.', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto menciona que um supermercado abriu perto e vendia pão mais barato, o que fez muitos clientes pararem de ir à padaria.","options":["The oven broke down","A supermarket offered cheaper bread","The baker got sick","The town''s population decreased"],"prompt":"Why did the bakery begin to struggle?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Ana sugeriu usar as redes sociais para atrair clientes, mostrando o processo de fabricação do pão e contando a história da padaria.","options":["To close the business","To reduce prices","To use social media","To hire more employees"],"prompt":"What was Ana''s initial suggestion to help the bakery?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A princípio, Sr. Carlos ficou cético e se perguntou por que alguém se interessaria por uma padaria simples na internet.","options":["He got very excited","He was doubtful","He refused immediately","He agreed without thinking"],"prompt":"How did Sr. Carlos react to Ana''s idea at first?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Depois da matéria na TV, muitas pessoas começaram a visitar a padaria e pedidos para eventos especiais começaram a chegar.","options":["The bakery closed","Sales increased","The bread got worse","The supermarket complained"],"prompt":"What happened after the local news featured the bakery?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Sr. Carlos planeja passar o negócio para Ana, que tem muitas ideias inovadoras, e ele confia que a padaria continuará fazendo parte da história da cidade.","options":["To retire and travel","To sell the bakery","To pass the business to Ana","To open another bakery"],"prompt":"What does Sr. Carlos plan for the future?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A história mostra que, mesmo com medo, tentar coisas novas pode ajudar a superar desafios, como Sr. Carlos fez ao usar a internet e a mídia para salvar a padaria.","options":["Old businesses always fail","Trying new things can be beneficial","Social media is only for young people","It''s better to give up when facing problems"],"prompt":"According to the text, what lesson can be learned from this story?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
