insert into public.reading_passages (id, language, level, title, body, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-reading-en-b1-07dd9399ad6e', 'en', 'B1', 'The Cave of Shadows', 'Last summer, I visited a cave in the mountains with my friends. We had heard stories about a hidden underground lake, and we wanted to find it. The cave was dark and cold, and the path was narrow. We walked carefully, using flashlights. After about an hour, we reached a large chamber. The walls sparkled with minerals, and in the center, there was a beautiful, still lake. We were amazed. We had never seen anything like it.

My friend Pedro had been to the cave before, so he knew the way. He told us that the lake was called the ''Mirror of the Sky'' because the water was so clear that it reflected the ceiling perfectly. We sat by the lake and ate our sandwiches. Suddenly, we heard a strange noise. It sounded like a deep growl. We froze. Then, we laughed when we realized it was just a bat flying overhead. We had been scared for nothing.

After we finished eating, we decided to explore further. We walked through a narrow tunnel and found another chamber. This one was smaller, but the floor was covered with sand. In the middle, there was a small hole in the ceiling, and a beam of sunlight came through, creating a spotlight effect. It was magical. I took a lot of photos.

However, time passed quickly, and we knew we had to leave before it got dark. Pedro said, ''We should go back now. It takes two hours to exit.'' We agreed. We turned off our flashlights to save battery and started walking back. But the path seemed different. We made a wrong turn and ended up in a dead end. Panic started to set in.

Then, I remembered that I had left a trail of small stones on the way in. I had seen it in a movie and thought it would be useful. We followed the stones and found our way back. When we finally saw the entrance, we cheered. We had been lost for almost an hour, but we learned a valuable lesson: always mark your path.

That experience taught me that even when you feel scared, staying calm and using your head can solve problems. Now, whenever I go hiking, I always carry a compass and tell someone where I''m going. I also never forget to leave a trail. It''s a simple trick that can save your life.

What about you? Have you ever been lost or in a scary situation? How did you handle it?', '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz ''I visited a cave in the mountains with my friends''.","options":["To a mountain","To a cave","To a lake","To a forest"],"prompt":"Where did the narrator and friends go last summer?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz ''in the center, there was a beautiful, still lake''.","options":["A hidden lake","A sleeping bear","An old treasure","A small hole"],"prompt":"What did they find in the large chamber?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz ''we laughed when we realized it was just a bat flying overhead''.","options":["Because it was a friend","Because it was a bat","Because it was a joke","Because it was a echo"],"prompt":"Why did they laugh when they heard the noise?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz ''we followed the stones and found our way back''.","options":["They used a map","They followed the stones","They called for help","They remembered the way"],"prompt":"How did they find their way back after getting lost?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz ''staying calm and using your head can solve problems''.","options":["Always bring a flashlight","Stay calm and use your head","Never go to caves","Travel with a guide"],"prompt":"What lesson did the narrator learn from the experience?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"O texto diz ''I always carry a compass and tell someone where I''m going''.","options":["Carries a compass and tells someone","Takes a map and a phone","Wears bright clothes","Leaves a trail of bread"],"prompt":"What did the narrator do now before hiking?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
