insert into public.quick_lessons (id, language, level, title, body, question, options, answer_index, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b1-5238299718d0', 'en', 'B1', 'Modals: Deduction, Obligation, Advice', 'Modal verbs are small but powerful words in English. They help us express possibility, necessity, and give advice. In this lesson, we will focus on three main uses: deduction (making guesses), obligation (expressing rules or duties), and advice (suggesting what someone should do).

For deduction, we use ''must'', ''might'', and ''can''t''. When we are almost sure something is true, we use ''must''. For example, if you see a man in a suit carrying a briefcase at 8 a.m., you might say, “He must be going to work.” If we think something is possible but not certain, we use ''might'' or ''may''. For instance, “She might be at home now, but I''m not sure.” When you are sure something is not true, we use ''can''t''. If a friend says, “I saw a lion in the street,” you might reply, “You can''t be serious! Lions don''t live here.”

For obligation, we use ''must'' and ''have to''. Both mean it is necessary, but there''s a subtle difference. ''Have to'' usually expresses an external obligation, like a rule or a law. For example, “You have to wear a seatbelt in a car.” ''Must'' is more internal, something you feel strongly about. For example, “I must call my mother today.” In the negative, ''mustn''t'' means it is forbidden, while ''don''t have to'' means it is not necessary. For instance, “You mustn''t smoke here” (it''s prohibited) versus “You don''t have to come to the meeting if you''re busy” (it''s optional).

For advice, we use ''should'' and ''ought to''. They are similar and can be used interchangeably. For example, “You should eat more vegetables” or “You ought to see a doctor if you feel sick.” ''Should'' is very common, and ''ought to'' is a bit more formal. In the negative, ''shouldn''t'' is used to suggest that something is not a good idea. For instance, “You shouldn''t stay up too late.”

Now, let''s see these modals in action. Imagine you are in a new city and you want to find a good restaurant. You might say, “We should ask a local for a recommendation.” If you see a long line at a place, you might think, “The food must be good.” On the other hand, if you see a restaurant with no customers, you might say, “It can''t be very good.” Later, you realize you forgot your wallet. You could say, “I must go back to the hotel to get it.” But your friend says, “You don''t have to go back; I can lend you some money.”

Here''s a short text to practice. Maria is a student from Brazil. She is planning a trip to London. She has a tight budget. “I must find a cheap hostel,” she thinks. “I might not be able to afford a nice hotel.” Her friend Paulo advises, “You should book your flight early to get a good price. You can''t miss the British Museum; it''s free.” Maria replies, “I might not have time to see everything, but I’ll try.” She also knows that in the UK, people have to drive on the left side of the road. She is glad she doesn''t have to drive there.

In summary, modals are useful tools. Use ''must'' and ''can''t'' when you are certain, ''might'' when you are not. Use ''must'' and ''have to'' for rules, and ''should'' for advice. Practice using them in your daily life, and you will become more confident in English.', 'What does ''must'' express in a sentence like ''He must be tired''?', '["A logical deduction","A rule","A piece of advice","A possibility"]'::jsonb, 0, '[{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"''Must'' é usado para fazer uma dedução lógica quando temos certeza de algo. No exemplo, ''He must be tired'' indica que deduzimos que ele está cansado.","options":["A logical deduction","A rule","A piece of advice","A possibility"],"prompt":"What does ''must'' express in a sentence like ''He must be tired''?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''Might'' é usado para expressar possibilidade. Significa que algo é possível, mas não certo.","options":["must","might","have to","should"],"prompt":"Which modal is used to express possibility?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''Mustn''t'' é usado para proibições. Indica que algo não é permitido.","options":["you don''t have to","you mustn''t","you shouldn''t","you mightn''t"],"prompt":"What is the correct way to express a prohibition?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"''Should'' é o modal mais comum para dar conselhos. É usado para sugerir o que é bom fazer.","options":["have to","must","should","can''t"],"prompt":"When giving advice, which modal is most common?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
