values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b1-a6ec4afa5b2b', 'en', 'B1', 'Passive Voice Basics in English', 'In English, we often talk about actions and who does them. For example, ''The chef cooks the food.'' But sometimes, we want to focus on the action itself or the receiver of the action, not the person who does it. That''s when we use the passive voice. For instance, ''The food is cooked by the chef.'' Here, the food is the subject, and the chef is mentioned at the end.

Why use the passive voice? It''s useful when the doer is unknown, obvious, or not important. For example, ''My car was stolen last night.'' We don''t know who stole it. Or ''The house was built in 1990.'' We don''t know or care who built it. In news reports and formal writing, the passive is common to sound objective.

How to form it? The passive uses the verb ''to be'' (am, is, are, was, were, been) plus the past participle of the main verb. For example: ''The email is sent.'' (present simple passive), ''The email was sent.'' (past simple passive). In the present, we use ''is/are'' + past participle; in the past, ''was/were'' + past participle. To change a sentence to passive, the object becomes the subject, and the doer is often introduced with ''by''.

Let''s look at a conversation. Maria: ''Who makes the coffee in your office?'' John: ''The coffee is made by the receptionist.'' Maria: ''And who cleans the office?'' John: ''It''s cleaned by a service every night.'' In these examples, the focus is on the coffee and the office, not on the people.

Now, here''s a quick tip: if you want to avoid mentioning the doer, you can use the passive without ''by''. For example, ''The window was broken.'' (We don''t say by whom.) This is common in everyday speech.

Let''s practice with a short story. Yesterday, a new café was opened in our neighborhood. The coffee is served in eco-friendly cups. Many people were invited to the opening, but only a few came. The pastries were baked by a local bakery. At the end of the day, everything was sold out!

Now, you try to identify the passive sentences. Remember, the passive is formed with ''to be'' + past participle. A common mistake is to use the past participle as a verb without ''be''. For example, ''The cake eaten.'' is wrong; you need ''The cake is eaten.'' or ''The cake was eaten.'' Another mistake is to forget the past participle form of irregular verbs, like ''written'' not ''wrote''.

Keep practicing, and you''ll soon see the passive voice is just a tool to change the focus of your message.', 'Which sentence is in the passive voice?', '["The chef cooks the food.","The food is cooked by the chef.","The chef is cooking the food.","The food cooks the chef."]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A frase ''The food is cooked by the chef'' está na voz passiva porque o sujeito (the food) recebe a ação, e o agente (by the chef) é introduzido por ''by''. As outras opções estão na voz ativa.","options":["The chef cooks the food.","The food is cooked by the chef.","The chef is cooking the food.","The food cooks the chef."],"prompt":"Which sentence is in the passive voice?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"No passado simples, usamos ''was'' ou ''were'' + particípio passado, como em ''The cake was baked.'' As outras opções são para outros tempos.","options":["is/are + past participle","was/were + past participle","have/has + past participle","will + be + past participle"],"prompt":"How is the passive voice formed in the past simple?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A opção ''The window was broken.'' é passiva e foca na ação sem mencionar quem a fez. As outras estão na voz ativa ou não são passivas.","options":["Someone broke the window.","The window was broken.","The window broke.","They broke the window."],"prompt":"Which sentence correctly uses the passive voice to focus on the action, not the doer?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A frase no passado simples ativo ''Maria wrote the report'' vira passiva com ''was written'' (passado de ''be'' + particípio passado de ''write''). ''Is written'' seria presente. ''Has been written'' é presente perfeito, e ''was wrote'' é erro gramatical.","options":["The report is written by Maria.","The report was written by Maria.","The report has been written by Maria.","The report was wrote by Maria."],"prompt":"What is the correct passive form of the sentence: ''Maria wrote the report.''?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
