insert into public.quick_lessons (id, language, level, title, body, question, options, answer_index, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b1-2a9b82e162d8', 'en', 'B1', 'Connecting Stories: Using Discourse Markers in English Narratives', 'When we tell a story, we don''t just put sentences one after another. We need to connect our ideas so that the listener can follow the sequence of events. In English, we use special words and phrases called discourse markers to show the order of events, contrast ideas, and add information. For example, we use ''firstly'', ''then'', ''after that'', ''finally'' to organize the steps of a story. We use ''however'' or ''but'' to show contrast, and ''so'' or ''therefore'' to show a result. In this lesson, you learned about these markers and how to use them effectively. Now, let''s practice with a short story about a visit to a new restaurant. Read the story and answer the questions.

Last weekend, I decided to try a new restaurant in my neighborhood. Firstly, I checked the reviews online and they were very positive. Then, I called to make a reservation. After that, I got ready and went to the restaurant. When I arrived, the place was full and I had to wait for thirty minutes. However, the wait was worth it because the food was delicious. I ordered a traditional Brazilian dish, and the presentation was beautiful. So, I took a photo to share with my friends. Finally, I finished my meal and paid the bill. Although it was a bit expensive, I left the restaurant feeling happy. Afterwards, I walked home and thought about the perfect evening.

Using these markers makes your storytelling clear and interesting. Remember to use a comma after markers like ''however'', ''firstly'', and ''afterwards'' when they start a sentence. This tiny detail helps the reader understand the structure. Now, let''s test your understanding with a few questions.
', 'What is the main purpose of discourse markers in a narrative?', '["To make sentences longer","To connect ideas and show relationships","To replace nouns","To make the story more difficult"]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Os marcadores discursivos são usados para conectar ideias, mostrar ordem, contraste e resultado, tornando a narrativa mais clara.","options":["To make sentences longer","To connect ideas and show relationships","To replace nouns","To make the story more difficult"],"prompt":"What is the main purpose of discourse markers in a narrative?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"''Firstly'' é usado para indicar o primeiro passo de uma sequência. ''However'' indica contraste, ''Finally'' indica o último passo e ''So'' indica resultado.","options":["However","Finally","Firstly","So"],"prompt":"Which marker is used to introduce the first step in a series?"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"''However'' é usado para introduzir uma ideia contrastante, como na frase ''However, the wait was worth it''.","options":["After that","However","Then","Finally"],"prompt":"In the story, which marker introduces a contrast?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"''So'' é usado para mostrar uma consequência ou resultado. No texto, ''So, I took a photo'' indica que ele tirou uma foto porque a comida estava bonita.","options":["A result","A contrast","A sequence","A conclusion"],"prompt":"What does the marker ''so'' indicate in the story?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
