insert into public.quick_lessons (id, language, level, title, body, question, options, answer_index, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b1-25426c78b4fa', 'en', 'B1', 'The Passive Voice in English', 'Have you ever noticed that in news reports, the focus is often on the action itself, not on who did it? For example, you might hear ''A new bridge was built in the city'' instead of ''The city built a new bridge.'' This is the passive voice. In English, we use the passive voice when the action is more important than the person who does it, or when we don''t know who did it. For brazilian learners, this is a common structure, but it can be tricky because it is formed differently from Portuguese.

In English, the passive voice is formed with the verb ''to be'' and the past participle of the main verb. For example, ''The cake was eaten by the children.'' Here, ''was'' is the past tense of ''to be'', and ''eaten'' is the past participle of ''eat''. The object of the active sentence becomes the subject of the passive sentence. The person who does the action (the agent) can be mentioned with ''by'', but it is often omitted if it is obvious or not important.

Let''s look at some examples. Active: ''Someone stole my car.'' Passive: ''My car was stolen.'' In the passive sentence, we don''t know who stole the car, so we don''t mention the agent. Active: ''Shakespeare wrote Hamlet.'' Passive: ''Hamlet was written by Shakespeare.'' Here, we keep the agent because it is important information.

We also use the passive voice in formal writing, such as academic articles or business reports. For example, ''It was decided that the project would be postponed.'' This sounds more objective. In conversation, we often prefer the active voice because it is more direct and personal.

However, avoid using the passive voice too much. It can make your writing sound weak and indirect. For instance, instead of saying ''A mistake was made by me,'' it is better to say ''I made a mistake.'' The passive voice is useful, but we should use it wisely.

Now, let''s practice with some questions.', 'Which sentence is in the passive voice?', '["The company launched a new product.","The new product was launched.","The new product sold well.","The company will launch a product."]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A frase ''The new product was launched'' está na voz passiva porque o sujeito ''the new product'' recebe a ação (foi lançado). As outras estão na voz ativa.","options":["The company launched a new product.","The new product was launched.","The new product sold well.","The company will launch a product."],"prompt":"Which sentence is in the passive voice?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Quando a ação está acontecendo agora, usamos ''is being + past participle''. Portanto, ''The road is being repaired'' é a forma correta.","options":["The road is repaired.","The road was being repaired.","The road is being repaired.","The road repairs."],"prompt":"Choose the correct passive form of the sentence: ''They are repairing the road.''"},{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"Em notícias, a voz passiva é comum para focar na ação. ''Taxes were raised by the government'' coloca ênfase no aumento dos impostos.","options":["Government raises taxes.","Taxes were raised by the government.","Citizens protest against taxes.","The economy is growing."],"prompt":"In a news article, which headline is more likely to use the passive voice?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"A frase ''The manager signed the contract'' está na voz ativa porque o sujeito (manager) realiza a ação. As outras são passivas.","options":["The letter was sent yesterday.","The report will be finished by Friday.","The manager signed the contract.","The song is being recorded."],"prompt":"Which sentence is NOT in the passive voice?"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
