insert into public.quick_lessons (id, language, level, title, body, question, options, answer_index, questions, sort_order, is_published)
values ('generated-quick-lesson-en-b1-b4cd6c059410', 'en', 'B1', 'Passive Voice Basics', 'The passive voice is used when we want to focus on the action or the receiver of the action, not on who does it. It is very common in news reports, scientific texts, and formal writing. In English, we form the passive voice with the verb ''to be'' and the past participle of the main verb. For example, ''The cake was eaten by the children.'' In this sentence, the focus is on the cake, not on who ate it.

We use the passive voice when the doer of the action is unknown, obvious, or not important. For instance, ''My car was stolen last night.'' We don''t know who stole it, so we use the passive. Or, ''The tests are graded by the teacher.'' Here, we want to emphasize the tests, not the teacher.

In Brazilian Portuguese, you also have the passive voice, but the structure is different. In English, we use ''to be'' + past participle, while in Portuguese, you can use ''ser'' or ''estar'' + past participle. For example, ''O bolo foi comido pelas crianças.'' Notice that the agent (by the children) is introduced with ''by'' in English and ''por'' in Portuguese.

When we want to say who does the action, we use ''by'' + the agent. For example, ''The book was written by a famous author.'' Sometimes, we can omit the agent if it is not important. For example, ''The window was broken.'' We don''t say by whom because it is not necessary.

A common mistake is to use the passive when the active voice is more appropriate. The passive can sound formal or impersonal, so in everyday conversation, we usually use the active voice. For example, we say ''Someone broke the window'' instead of ''The window was broken by someone.''

Let''s practice with some examples. Look at the sentence: ''The company produces eco-friendly products.'' The active voice focuses on the company. To make it passive, we say: ''Eco-friendly products are produced by the company.'' Notice that the object of the active sentence (products) becomes the subject of the passive sentence.

Remember, the passive voice is not a tense; it can be used in different tenses. For example, ''The house is built'' (present), ''The house was built'' (past), and ''The house will be built'' (future). The tense depends on the verb ''to be''.

Now, let''s check your understanding with some questions.', 'Which sentence is in the passive voice?', '["The chef cooked a delicious meal.","A delicious meal was cooked by the chef.","The chef is cooking a delicious meal.","The chef will cook a delicious meal."]'::jsonb, 1, '[{"answer_index":1,"explanation_pt_br":"A frase ''A delicious meal was cooked by the chef'' usa a estrutura ''was cooked'' (verbo to be no passado + particípio passado), caracterizando a voz passiva.","options":["The chef cooked a delicious meal.","A delicious meal was cooked by the chef.","The chef is cooking a delicious meal.","The chef will cook a delicious meal."],"prompt":"Which sentence is in the passive voice?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"Na voz passiva, o objeto ''Portuguese'' vira sujeito, e usamos o verbo ''to be'' no presente (is) + particípio passado ''spoken''.","options":["Portuguese is spoken in Brazil.","Portuguese was spoken in Brazil.","Portuguese has spoken in Brazil.","Portuguese is speaking in Brazil."],"prompt":"What is the correct passive form of ''They speak Portuguese in Brazil''?"},{"answer_index":2,"explanation_pt_br":"Na voz passiva, o foco está na ação ou no receptor, não em quem a realizou. Por isso, é comum em notícias, onde o importante é o fato.","options":["To emphasize the doer of the action.","To make the text more emotional.","To focus on the action or result.","To make the text longer."],"prompt":"Why do we often use the passive voice in news reports?"},{"answer_index":0,"explanation_pt_br":"No futuro, usamos ''will be'' + particípio passado. Assim, ''will be opened'' está correto.","options":["The new museum will be opened next month.","The new museum will open next month.","The new museum is opened next month.","The new museum was opened next month."],"prompt":"Choose the correct passive sentence for ''They will open the new museum next month.''"}]'::jsonb, 0, true)
